\subsection{Primary Outcomes}

\textbf{Time-to-correct-information:} CMA significantly reduced the time required to retrieve correct information compared to standard search. Median time-to-correct-information was 96.4 seconds (IQR 72.1--128.5) in the CMA condition versus 118.2 seconds (IQR 89.3--156.7) in the control condition, representing an 18.6\% relative reduction (95\% CI: 9.2\%--27.1\%, p=0.0003). The mixed-effects model yielded a log-scale coefficient of $\beta_1 = -0.206$ (95\% CI: $-0.314$ to $-0.098$), equivalent to an 18.8\% decrease. Effect size (Cohen's d) was computed as:

\begin{equation}
d = \frac{\overline{X}_{\text{control}} - \overline{X}_{\text{CMA}}}{\sqrt{\frac{(n_1-1)s_1^2 + (n_2-1)s_2^2}{n_1 + n_2 - 2}}} = 0.51
\end{equation}

indicating a moderate and clinically meaningful improvement.

